      {
        "id": 90248,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T05:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Your math does indeed look correct to me.&nbsp; Every time Zero dishes out an instance of damage, he gets +1 from Galvanize, and another +1 from Apertures if the damage type is Cold.&nbsp; Galvanize + Transducer is always fun, though Galvanize + Shockwave is not necessarily so.</p><p>One thing to keep in mind with AZ...if the fire damage from Thermal Shockwave kills him, he gets no option to use Transducer.&nbsp; But as long as he survives, here's a tip: if you have his other Module in play as well, the Transducer's outgoing cold damage may target AZ to heal him.&nbsp; Without any +1s to your damage, this basically makes AZ immune to any nonlethal amount of fire damage; with a +1, using Thermodynamics to deal 2 fire to yourself and then heal for 3 (or 4 if you have Apertures) with the Transduced cold damage is a very effective strategy.&nbsp; Cryo Chamber makes it even better, as long as you have that +1, since you then can deal a net of 1 fire damage to yourself and get back as much as 4 HP in return (you still need Apertures to hit 4, since your cold damage is up to +3 but your original fire damage was one less than without the Cryo Chamber).</p><p>AZ and Legacy really like to hang around together!</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:15:31.053Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
